WHPG Real Streaming Demo — Restart Guide
Quick reference for stopping, resetting, and restarting the Forrester/WHPG streaming demo (E-commerce + IoT + TU CDC pipeline).
1. Connect to the box
ssh ec2-user@<host>
su - gpadmin
cd forrester/repo/scripts
2. Choose your restart path
Option A — Full reset (recommended for a clean demo run)
Stops everything, drops/recreates tables, resets ClickHouse, resets the CDC pipeline, then starts everything fresh with a health check.

./reset-demo-cdc.sh --region <region>

Example used previously:

./reset-demo-cdc.sh --region egypt

This single command does all of the following for you:

Stops FlowServer, jobs, generators, and the dashboard API
Drops + recreates ecommerce_orders and iot_sensor_readings
Resets the ClickHouse ecommerce-orders mirror
Resets the TU CDC pipeline (Postgres → Debezium → Kafka → WarehousePG)
Starts everything fresh (generators, FlowServer jobs, dashboard API)
Runs a full health check on all services
Option B — Simple stop/start (no data reset)
If you just need to bounce the demo without wiping data:

./stop-demo.sh
./start-demo.sh
3. After a reset — manual step required
⚠️ The reset script does NOT restart the CDC FlowServer jobs automatically. After topics are recreated, go to the FlowServer UI and resubmit/restart:

tu_load_credit_accounts
tu_load_bureau_score_events
4. Verify it's up
Check the URLs:

Dashboard: http://localhost:5055/
FlowServer: http://localhost:6060/

Or tail the logs:

tail -f /tmp/flowserver-demo/logs/*.log

The reset script's own health check confirms:

Kafka broker reachable (port 9092)
Debezium connect-standalone running + replication slot debezium_tu_slot active
FlowServer reachable (port 6060), order-generator and iot-generator running
dashboard-api running
ClickHouse reachable (port 9094), with default.ecommerce_orders row count climbing as the topic refills
5. Notes / gotchas
Generators run at 10,000/s for both e-commerce orders and IoT sensor data by default.
The --region flag controls the e-commerce order generator's region (e.g. egypt).
"Not found" / "no PID file" messages during the stop phase of a reset are expected if nothing was running — the script treats these as OK, not errors.
Kafka topics ecommerce-orders and iot-sensors-csv are deleted and recreated as part of a full reset.
TU Kafka topics (tu.oltp.credit_accounts, tu.oltp.bureau_score_events) are also deleted/recreated — this is why the FlowServer CDC jobs need to be manually resubmitted afterward (Step 3 above).
